  "id": "COMPOUND:2477 - PROTEIN:5796",
  "verbalization": "Latrunculin A is implicated in the regulation of SNU-387, a cell line that is targeted by multiple compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, Dendocarbin K, and Licochalcone D. These compounds all share a common target, CX-1, suggesting a potential pathway where Latrunculin A influences the activity of SNU-387, which in turn affects CX-1. The evidence indicates that Latrunculin A may act as a modulator of SNU-387, potentially through a shared mechanism that leads to the activation or inhibition of CX-1. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple compounds targeting SNU-387 and their shared effect on CX-1 implies a broader regulatory network, possibly involving cellular signaling pathways that are not yet fully understood.",
